# /etc/mw-deadman.pins  on each checker host (root:root, 0600)
# DO NOT hand-write. Generated by:  mw-deadman-check.sh pin --yes
# (run it only AFTER you've confirmed the watched host is clean). One "key<TAB>sha256" per line.
# Re-run pin --yes after EVERY legitimate change to the watcher/units/env/baseline,
# otherwise the next check will alarm on your own edit.
#
# Example shape (hashes illustrative):
# watch	3f2a…realhash…
# hb	9b17…
# resp	c40e…
# svc	7d55…
# timer	1aa9…
# hbsvc	b2c8…
# hbtimer	e6f1…
# harden	44d0…
# env	a19c…        <- sha256 of /etc/malware-watch.env (its HASH, never its contents)
# baseline	5e7b…    <- fingerprint of the whole baseline dir
# mwpull_ak	0c93…   <- watched host /home/mwpull/.ssh/authorized_keys (detects added keys / changed forced cmd)
# auditd	f8a2…       <- /etc/audit/rules.d/mw.rules
# sudoers	2b6d…      <- /etc/sudoers.d/mw-pull
